WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
Tesla's roadster teaser image flips to reveal rocket thrusters and the hidden phrase, where we're

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:13.360
going, ahead of the October 1st debut. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 604. Tesla is regaining

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:19.640
ground in the US electric vehicle market, while several legacy manufacturers scale back. Market

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:25.740
data shows Tesla increasing its share of new EV registrations in recent months. Legacy

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:31.540
automakers cited softening demand and higher costs as reasons for slowing production or delaying

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:37.560
new models. Tesla's pricing and software features are described as key factors helping it capture

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:43.340
buyers who might otherwise have considered other brands. While software helps move current vehicles,

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:50.140
Tesla is also teasing what comes after the conventional car. Tesla full self-driving capability is

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:56.040
reported as a factor behind rising vehicle sales in North America. Sales data referenced in the

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:01.660
report shows an uptick in North American deliveries coinciding with software updates that improved city

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:07.900
street performance. Fleet operators and individual buyers are described as citing the software as a

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:13.580
deciding factor when choosing between Tesla and competing electric models. The article notes that

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:20.460
FSD remains a paid upgrade option on new vehicles. Flipping the teaser image upside down reveals the

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:26.400
rear of a hypercar with rocket thruster plumes. Adjusting exposure and shadows in the dark strip

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:32.860
between the tail light and thrusters uncovers the text, where we're going. The image is stamped with

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:41.100
10.01. Every sci-fi fan knows the rest of Doc Brown's iconic line. Roads, where we're going, we don't

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:47.940
need roads. Tesla stamped 10.01 on the image, but the message in the dark said the era of the

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:54.340
conventional supercar is officially dead. Big picture product teases often sit alongside the day-to-day

00:01:54.340 --> 00:02:00.120
realities of the existing lineup. The model Y remains the top-selling electric vehicle in America,

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:06.960
even as reviewers highlight specific shortcomings. The article examines ride quality, interior materials,

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:13.460
and build tolerances as areas where the vehicle falls short of some competitors. Despite those critiques,

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:19.140
registration data shows the model Y outselling every other EV nameplate by a wide margin.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:25.200
The piece notes that software updates and available range continue to outweigh the listed drawbacks

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:31.600
for many buyers. The same production muscle that keeps model Y dominant is also preparing for heavier

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:37.580
commercial duty. Production and delivery plans for the electric semi in Europe are now targeted for

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:43.140
the following year. The timeline follows regulatory approval work and infrastructure assessments

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:49.140
in several EU countries. The article references earlier statements that the European version would

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:54.480
differ in battery configuration from the North American model. Customer fleet discussions are

00:02:54.600 --> 00:03:01.140
described as ongoing ahead of the 2027 start. While the semi waits for Europe, the charging

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:07.000
network keeps expanding in the US. Tesla installed chargers at a cracker barrel location after

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:13.180
earlier plans for an iHOP site were changed. The site adds 4 stalls to the network in the Dalton

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:20.000
area. Rates are noted as lower than nearby Chattanooga and Calhoun sites. Users report the location

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:26.760
fills a long-standing gap on routes between Atlanta and Chattanooga. Every day network growth contrasts

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:32.780
with bigger questions about how drivers actually use the software on those roads. Official owner manual

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:39.080
updates indicate text messaging via GROC will be added to NCAB and capabilities. The documentation

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:43.640
lists the feature as an upcoming addition to the existing voice and visual interface.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:48.880
The manual entry appears in the latest version available to owners checking release notes.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:53.000
No specific rollout date is listed in the current documentation.

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:58.920
NCAB and AI features are one thing. Real-world supervised driving behavior is another.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:03.860
Multiple drivers describe the system waiting too long at exits before rerouting.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.780
The pattern appears across separate vehicles and software versions.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:13.560
Owners report the behavior occurring on familiar routes where previous versions had taken the correct

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:19.100
exit. Tesla has not yet issued a specific software response to the reported behavior.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:25.320
Battery cell chemistry and pack architecture decisions determine far more than range figures on a

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:32.320
spec sheet. Tesla's shift toward 4680 cells with structural integration changes how energy density,

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:37.220
thermal paths, and manufacturing tolerances interact on the same assembly line.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:41.640
Conventional pack designs separate the cell array from the vehicle chassis,

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:47.200
allowing independent optimization of each subsystem but adding mass and connection points.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:53.160
Structural packs collapse those layers, forcing every tolerance decision to satisfy both

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:59.400
electrical and mechanical requirements simultaneously. When a single stamping operation forms both

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.840
the battery enclosure and the vehicle floor, the capital equipment must deliver surface finish and

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:08.680
dimensional accuracy that used to be handled by two separate suppliers.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:14.220
Yield losses at that station now affect both battery capacity and body rigidity,

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:19.500
creating a tighter feedback loop between cell manufacturing and final vehicle quality.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.580
Looking back over the past week, three threads stood out across the coverage.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:31.160
Megapack production ramped with a new giga Texas line adding 50 gigawatt hours of annual utility

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:37.840
scale storage capacity, and an $800 million deal with zero brought three gigawatt hours to Italy.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:45.180
Sales pressure continued in China after a 12.4% drop in August, leaving Tesla needing a record

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:51.260
September to meet quarterly targets. Hardware reveals lined up around the dedicated semi-factory

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:55.960
showcase set for September 24, and the Roadster debut on October 1.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:01.440
Before we go, the next software version is already showing further gains in intersection

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:10.200
handling during internal testing. That's your Tesla news for today. TSLA closed at $365.44,

